<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krujë</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kruja, Croia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krujë is a town in north-central Albania, on a mountainside above the coastal plain. In the late 12th century it was the centre of Arbanon, the first Albanian principality. Its castle became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>'s stronghold in his war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and withstood sieges in 1450, 1466 and 1467 before falling in 1478. A museum dedicated to Skanderbeg stands inside the castle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kruje.jpg" alt="Krujë" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Chris Walts · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kruj%C3%AB-KrujaAlbania_2016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
